"""Write the report from finished, verified outcomes only."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
read=lambda name:json.loads((P/name).read_text())
a=read('ANALYSIS.json');n=read('TRAINING_RESULTS.json');v=read('RESULT_VERIFICATION.json');g=read('geometry/VERIFICATION.json')
assert v['status']==g['status']=='PASS'
lines=['# Plinius45: closing the native run and returning to the scroll','','The approved native profilometry trajectory completed 8,192 updates. The source and target audits support redirecting the programme to a PHerc343 positive-control reproduction and then PHerc0800. Further profilometry studies and the unsent Paris4 reference request are shelved. A CPU AP gain is no longer a universal prerequisite for a properly designed GPU pilot; the £10 total cap and concrete launch controls remain.','','## Native continuation','','The first 2,048 updates reproduced every one of 42 original model tensors exactly. Training then continued for 6,144 additional updates without resetting AdamW or either random generator. Model, optimizer moments/counts and RNG state were retained and read back at 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192. Architecture, inputs, weighted BCE, sampling and learning rate were unchanged. This was one fold, training PHerc250/500P2; the PHerc248 development scores did not choose its endpoint.','','| Updates | PHerc250 training AP | PHerc500P2 training AP |','|---:|---:|---:|']
for row in n['training_fit']:
    d={c['case'].split('_')[0]:c['metrics']['ap'] for c in row['cases']};lines.append(f'|{row["step"]}|{d["250"]:.6f}|{d["500P2"]:.6f}|')
status=a['native']['budget_interpretation'];growth=a['native']['AP_growth_4096_to8192']
if status=='single_fold_fit_qualified':decision='Both training papyri reached the prespecified 0.80 AP criterion. This establishes fit for this fold and setup, not cross-papyrus or CT transfer. It does not automatically reopen the shelved profilometry programme.'
elif status=='fit_failed_flat_last_interval':decision='The 0.80AP fit criterion failed, and both training AP gains in the last interval were below 0.01. For this setup, the result weakens the explanation that a modest extension of this trajectory alone would solve fitting. It does not isolate objective, context, capacity, supervision or information loss.'
else:decision='The 0.80AP fit criterion failed, while at least one training AP still improved by 0.01 or more in the last interval. Optimization budget remains inconclusive for this setup. The result does not establish a lack of recoverable information; the strategic decision is to stop this supporting branch and return to the target.'
lines+=['',decision,'','Final-interval gains: '+', '.join(f'{k}: {d:+.6f}AP' for k,d in growth.items())+'. The original positive-centre oversampling plus class weighting remains a probability-calibration caveat; AP is the fixed primary fit metric.','','PHerc248 was already exposed development data. Its fixed final scores are '+', '.join(f'{r["quality"]}: AP{r["metrics"]["ap"]:.6f}, AUC{r["metrics"]["auroc"]:.6f}' for r in n['reserved_development_evaluation'])+'. No untouched-test or CT-ink result is claimed.','','## Released-checkpoint variability','','Four fixed released checkpoints—seeds 42 and 43 at 60k and 75k—were evaluated on all eight reused regions. The seed42/75k repeat exactly reproduced all eight archived baseline arrays. There were 800 new single-tile forwards and no fitting or checkpoint selection. One initial role-label validation failure occurred before construction/forward; the additive correction is preserved.','','| Region | AP: seed43 minus seed42 at75k |','|---|---:|']
contrast=a['checkpoint_contrasts']['final_seed_difference']
for r in contrast['regions']:lines.append(f'|{r["id"]}|{r["delta"]["average_precision"]:+.6f}|')
lines+=['',f'The equal-parent Paris difference is **{contrast["Paris_equal_parent_delta"]["average_precision"]:+.6f}AP**; the maximum absolute regional difference is **{contrast["maximum_absolute_regional_AP"]:.6f}AP**, with{contrast["regions_absolute_AP_above_001"]}/8regions exceeding0.01in absolute AP. Late-checkpoint Paris changes (75k−60k) are '+', '.join(f'{seed}: {a["checkpoint_contrasts"][seed+"_late_training"]["Paris_equal_parent_delta"]["average_precision"]:+.6f}AP' for seed in ['seed42','seed43'])+'.','','These are descriptive released-checkpoint differences, not a calibrated noise floor. Two seeds and correlated temporal endpoints do not establish a reliable variance, statistical power or a twice-noise significance gate. The practical0.01margin and uncertainty must remain separate. The old Paris panel has only two physical parents and remains development/regression evidence. No model is promoted from this comparison.','','## Target geometry and new sources','','A fixed sparse lattice measured nearest-run disagreement with the public M7 prediction on three previously used PHerc0800 meshes. Median absolute offsets were0.5,1.0and1.0native voxels.20 / 102 measurable sites exceeded two voxels, two other sites tied between nearest sheets, and57 / 104 usable profiles contained multiple predicted runs. None of the three medians exceeds the old engineering threshold. This argues against blanket recentering; local outliers and wrap ambiguity remain worth testing. M7 agreement is not an independent measurement of true surface placement. See [the full geometry report](GEOMETRY_RESULTS.md).','','PHerc343 uses the target acquisition settings8.64 µm / 116 keV and supplies a concrete66-layer,±15-depth, four-model recipe including Hecate. Its mesh concatenation reproduced all three coordinate files and metadata byte for byte; its published image hash was verified. CT rendering and ink maps have **not** been reproduced here. Hecate needs9.6 µm sampling in all three axes and already implements paired fine-to-native supervision; that changes our prior-art baseline.','','Eleven live metadata reads confirmed PHerc0139 fine/native paired renders and the author benchmark/blank-control assets. The references are model-generated and local registration still requires checking, but this is a direct supporting route that need not wait on the Paris4 request.','','[Critical review and primary sources](STRATEGY_REVIEW.md) · [One next experiment and its stopping criteria](NEXT_STUDY_DRAFT.md) · [Overview](overview.png) · [Geometry lattice](geometry-offsets.png)','','## Verification and persistence','',f'Independent retained-output checks reproduced{v["ranking_values"]}ranking values (maximum difference{v["maximum_ranking_difference"]:.3g}), reconstructed all eight panel supports and blended{v["blended_score_pixels"]:,}pixels from800raw tiles (maximum difference{v["maximum_blend_difference"]:.3g}). Optimizer steps/moments and all three saved continuation states were checked. Separately, all104M7profiles were reconstructed from 71 observed chunks and their run classifications independently reproduced. These checks establish computational fidelity, not physical ink truth or experimental power.','','The native worker made8,192training minibatch forwards/backwards plus216evaluation minibatch forwards;2,048of its updates replay prior work. The checkpoint panel made800single-tile forwards. The actual CPU quota is four cores; simultaneous Torch workers caused severe contention, so the panel was paused with state intact and resumed after native training. No scientific trajectory was restarted to improve an outcome.','','GPU spend: **£0**. No paid resource, R2 upload, maintainer message, new reading or translation. Selected code/reports/metadata/figures are exported to GitHub; bulk arrays, chunks, maps and checkpoints remain in the cloud lab. See [portability and exact limits](PORTABILITY.md).']
prior=json.loads((P.parent/'fortyfourth-experiment/training/fold0-native-result.json').read_text())
before=next(r['metrics']['ap'] for r in prior['test'] if r['quality']=='native')
after=next(r['metrics']['ap'] for r in n['reserved_development_evaluation'] if r['quality']=='native')
insert=lines.index('## Released-checkpoint variability')
lines[insert:insert]=[f'On that reserved development papyrus, native-input AP changed from {before:.6f} at 2,048 updates to {after:.6f} at 8,192 ({after-before:+.6f}). The greater training fit did not transfer in this fold. This supports closing the branch while keeping the distinction between underfitting and transfer failure explicit.','']
with (P/'RESULTS.md').open('x') as f:f.write('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Verified results report written')
